    <h3 id="engineering-chassis-cycle1-build">Build</h3>
        <p>
          Following sgRNA design, the guide fragment was assembled into linearized pML104 via one-step cloning, followed by transformation into TOP10 and plating on LB-Amp plates (not shown). In parallel, linearized pML104, the guide fragment, and an approximately 600 bp repair template were co-transformed into BY4741 and plated on SD-His plates (Figure 1).
        </p>

    <h3 id="engineering-chassis-cycle1-test">Test</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Route A:</strong> No E. coli transformants were obtained, with no colonies on the LB-Amp plates, and thus no circular plasmid could be recovered for yeast transformation or subsequent validation experiments.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Route B:</strong> Colonies grew on the SD-His plates, but no knockout-positive clones were detected by colony PCR (Figure 2). Sanger sequencing of candidate clones showed that the target 4 bp sequence highlighted in yellow was still present, and the target site remained wild-type, confirming that no knockout had occurred (Figure 3).
        </p>
